1
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,680
Proceed to Pompeii.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,057
I have hidden a key somewhere
near the Cave Cana mosaic.

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:11,677
This hidden key will operate
the vehicle that'll allow

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:17,020
your team safe passage as you deliver
my daughter. Fugo! Abbacchio! Giorno!

5
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,399
You three will travel to
Pompeii to secure that key.

6
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,380
Thank you.

7
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:12,380
Thank you.

8
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:35,140
In my life, I won't be able to fight.

9
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:37,917
I'll continue to fight!

10
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,877
I will be

11
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:45,317
able to fight.

12
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,960
Fighting God?

13
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:56,157
Pompeii, ancient Roman resort
and city of culture and vitality.

14
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:59,740
When Mount Vesuvius erupted back in AD 79,

15
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:03,520
the city was ravaged by
fire and buried by ash.

16
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,240
It was a catastrophe.

17
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:11,068
Later, archaeologists discovered
a metropolis frozen in time.

18
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:12,837
Everything there was preserved.

19
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:16,273
Entire villas, wine bottles,
roads, even carriage tracks.

20
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:18,200
So you're aware,

21
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,417
the Cave Canem is a mosaic
of a dog located in the

22
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,559
vestibule of the so-called
House of the Tragic Poet.

23
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,300
Oh, Fugo.

24
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:34,736
It seems we needed to turn
right back there, not left.

25
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:41,057
Isn't it a little bit late
to be telling me that?

26
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:45,140
Tell me, what good does it do to
inform me of a turn after the fact?

27
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:48,020
You're absolutely right. I'm sorry.

28
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:49,379
Next time, I will.

29
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:52,200
Did I say anything about
next time, new kid?

30
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,577
I'm talking about now!

31
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:55,400
Check your emotions.

32
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:57,780
We're in a hurry, so calm down.

33
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,547
You don't think I know that?

34
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,320
It's annoying as shit,
but this is typical Fugo.

35
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:12,507
What's really bugging me is this
new recruit, Giorno Giovanna.

36
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:17,557
Uttarati wants us to treat him as one
of our own, so I'll do what I must.

37
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:21,464
But there's something about this
guy, something I can't get past.

38
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:28,160
Eventually, he's going to screw up big
time, and his blunder could get us killed.

39
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:34,237
Good old Pompei.

40
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:37,160
I haven't set foot
there since I was a kid.

41
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,500
Abacchio, Giorno, let's hustle.

42
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,344
Our destination is about
a hundred meters ahead.

43
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,757
It should take thirty minutes or so to get

44
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:58,311
what we need and hightail it back to camp!

45
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:08,120
Abbacchio, Giorno, eyes up.

46
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:11,287
Well, that didn't take long.

47
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:12,560
How many?

48
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,030
Just one.

49
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:15,572
At least for the moment.

50
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:18,057
He's watching us from behind that pillar.

51
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:21,440
And by that pillar, which
one do you mean exactly?

52
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,347
Open your damn eyes, Giorno.

53
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:25,137
There's only one pillar here.

54
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,837
You can't see it from there?

55
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:29,840
Fugo, you're definitely
right about the pillar.

56
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:32,660
But there's no one watching us.

57
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,597
I know what I'm looking at, damn it!

58
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,621
He's closing in!

59
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:39,920
Fugo! Right there!

60
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:41,611
He's sauntering this way!

61
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,600
I know I saw him.

62
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:48,408
A guy just came out
from behind that pillar.

63
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,735
I saw his every move with this mirror.

64
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:54,480
What the hell?

65
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:57,500
There he is! Look there! He came out!

66
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:04,020
Wait, is he skulking in the mirror?

67
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:08,420
He showed his stand!

68
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:09,510
One of you attacked!

69
00:05:09,593 --> 00:05:10,457
Hey, take a beat!

70
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:13,517
Nothing you've said in the last
few minutes has made any sense!

71
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,497
Wait, is something the
matter with the mirror?

72
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:16,410
Shit!

73
00:05:16,493 --> 00:05:17,677
He's coming in for the kill!

74
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:19,936
You have to get away from the mirror!

75
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:25,180
What? Giorno! Abokyo!

76
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,130
Where are you?

77
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:31,281
What's going on?

78
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,082
Where'd you go?

79
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,162
That mirror freak vanished, too.

80
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:38,770
What'd he do?

81
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:42,380
Of course the creepy hanging
mirror was a red flag.

82
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,377
How the hell did I fall for that?

83
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:46,020
What is this guy's stand?

84
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,320
How does it work?

85
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:51,020
Also, I don't know what it is, but...

86
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:55,520
Something about this place
just doesn't look right.

87
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:56,770
Xiao!

88
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,950
What?

89
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,777
Panna Code Fugo M.

90
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:12,040
Your IQ is 152, and you entered
university at the age of 13.

91
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:15,680
But a certain professor
rubbed you the wrong way,

92
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:19,724
so you decided to beat him to a
bloody pulp with an encyclopedia.

93
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:22,528
Frankly, the rest is a
depressing biography.

94
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:26,820
You're currently traveling with
the failed cop, Leone Abacchio,

95
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:30,840
as well as the lack of
data must mean he's new.

96
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:33,640
I believe you called him Giorno.

97
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,300
You bastard.

98
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:36,717
Tell me where they are.

99
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:37,700
Out with it.

100
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:39,417
Where did you put them?

101
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,460
Tell me now!

102
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:47,240
My watch is backwards.

103
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:51,308
And now it's on my right wrist,
which doesn't make any sense.

104
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:54,640
I get it. Damn you.

105
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,744
So that's what your stand does.

106
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:59,645
I knew you were quick,
but that was impressive.

107
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:01,880
I like your eagerness, Fugo.

108
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,577
I'll admit that I wasn't aiming for you,

109
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:07,277
but since you noticed the
mirror before the others,

110
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,580
you get to go first.

111
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:11,497
Abbacchio and Giorno didn't disappear.

112
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:13,840
This is some kind of mirror world.

113
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,400
I'm the victim here.

114
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:19,287
He dragged me into his
own little playground.

115
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:21,330
Fugo!

116
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:23,100
Come out already!

117
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:26,369
Giorno, didn't you see
anything suspicious?

118
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:28,460
Not sure.

119
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:31,961
One second I'm looking at
him, the next he's gone.

120
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:34,120
Fugo, where are you?

121
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:39,237
Right before he vanished, he warned
us to get away from the mirror.

122
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:43,085
He asked if we could see the man
walking from behind the pillar.

123
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:44,120
This mirror.

124
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:45,670
Strano.

125
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,737
Something's off about this mirror.

126
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:48,800
But what?

127
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:51,920
Now for the question at hand.

128
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:55,417
Where did you and your comrades
hide the boss's daughter?

129
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:58,912
Actually, I should say that's
the more important question.

130
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:03,697
My other question concerns why you goons
are snooping around the city of death.

131
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:07,309
That's the piece of this puzzle
I just can't seem to ignore.

132
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:11,857
It doesn't take a genius to figure out
you came here searching for something.

133
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,940
Whatever it is,

134
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:17,117
it would have to be vital to protecting
the girl to justify coming all this way,

135
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:18,030
right?

136
00:08:18,113 --> 00:08:22,200
Just around that corner, you'll
find the famous Cave Cana mosaic.

137
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:24,580
Is that where your prize lies?

138
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,620
Well, whatever it is, I'm taking it!

139
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:31,837
Now do yourself a favor and tell
me what this thing is, Fugo!

140
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:32,750
Eat shit!

141
00:08:32,833 --> 00:08:34,380
So you choose death, then!

142
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:36,560
Wrong, Stranzo!

143
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:40,197
That honor will go to you once
I unleash my stand's power!

144
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,220
Purple smoke!

145
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:48,180
It won't manifest. Why? I see.

146
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,860
Purple smoke, eh?

147
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,981
It's an interesting name
for your no-show ability.

148
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:57,469
I'm absolutely sure I
brought out my stand.

149
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,300
I can even feel its power.

150
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:01,140
So where the hell is it?

151
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:06,920
Hey, Giorno, I need you
to walk toward me slowly.

152
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:09,580
You need me to what?

153
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:12,160
Get your newbie ass over here!

154
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:13,477
We're running out of time!

155
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:14,390
Move it now!

156
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:17,790
What?

157
00:09:17,873 --> 00:09:18,703
Are we being attacked?

158
00:09:18,786 --> 00:09:19,616
No, kid!

159
00:09:19,699 --> 00:09:20,529
Stand down now!

160
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:21,837
That's not the enemy!

161
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:23,120
It's Fugo's stand!

162
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:27,472
Unless you want to die, quick
digging around and get back!

163
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:30,280
Fugos, move away from purple smoke!

164
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:31,580
Hurry, fool!

165
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:41,460
I suppose I should tell
you you're inside a mirror.

166
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:44,997
Do you know why I pulled you
in here all by your lonesome?

167
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,374
Hint, it's not for the peace and quiet.

168
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:49,437
It's cause bringing
along any of your fellow

169
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:52,057
combatants could put my
own safety in jeopardy.

170
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:54,020
and I just can't have that.

171
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:56,720
I control everything here.

172
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:58,460
That is my unique talent.

173
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:02,320
All you see before you is
devoid of life, fully inanimate.

174
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:05,037
We're the only living
things in this realm.

175
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,826
I made it a point to
keep everything else out.

176
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,120
I permitted your entry
because my plan needed you.

177
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:12,461
You catching on?

178
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:15,856
Your stand manifested on the
other side of the mirror!

179
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:18,760
Now feast your eyes upon my mirror man!

180
00:10:25,420 --> 00:10:27,900
Purple smoke materialized on the outside.

181
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:32,500
This is a nightmare, but there's
got to be a way I can fight back!

182
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:43,837
Panacota Fugo was born
into tremendous wealth

183
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:46,660
and lived on a vast estate outside Napoli.

184
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:51,340
He was blessed, not only with
a life of luxury and privilege,

185
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:54,157
but with a great intellect as well.

186
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:58,400
To many, he lived the perfect
life, devoid of any hardship.

187
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,197
But what the public didn't see were the

188
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:03,960
many expectations placed
on Fugo's shoulders.

189
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:07,860
The pressure from them was
crushing his spirit day by day.

190
00:11:11,260 --> 00:11:16,300
At times, Fugo suffered bouts of inexplicable
rage, which caused him to act out.

191
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:23,080
It was a deep anger that took
all his might to contain.

192
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:26,989
At the age of just 13,
he began university.

193
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:31,800
It was there that his near-uncontrollable
furor erupted into tragedy.

194
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:34,350
Fugo.

195
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:36,060
Oh, Professor.

196
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:39,380
Now what could you be up
to at this ungodly hour?

197
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,360
It's for our assignment.

198
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:43,578
I can't find the judicial precedent.

199
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:48,337
Oh don't be silly you
know that you can always

200
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:50,960
come to me with anything hard that arises.

201
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,917
No I wouldn't want to
trouble you if I don't

202
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,757
have to guiding gifted
young men like you is.

203
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:01,517
No trouble at all it's
my scholarly duty how

204
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:04,417
about it have dinner at
my place and I'll teach.

205
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:08,137
You a few things I have
to go now wait just a

206
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:11,217
moment I'd be more than
happy to loose my lips.

207
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:14,060
regarding the questions
on the next big test.

208
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:16,357
Everything's going to be just fine.

209
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:17,270
Stop it.

210
00:12:17,353 --> 00:12:18,183
Relax, you're in good hands.

211
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:22,074
Get your hands off me!

212
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,860
I looked up to you!

213
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:28,940
I wanted to be like you!

214
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:31,740
You disgusting piece of shit!

215
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:36,500
I heard Profissori's
getting real cozy with Fugo.

216
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:39,000
You sure Fugo didn't bait the hook?

217
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:42,696
That would explain how he
got into a school like this.

218
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:48,994
Fugo's parents leveraged their wealth
to ensure all charges were dropped.

219
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:54,242
But they no longer treated him like a son,
and he was no longer part of the family.

220
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:59,412
Without support, Fugo turned to
shoplifting and pickpocketing for survival.

221
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,860
In an ironic twist of fate,

222
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:05,897
it was his new way of life that
would make full use of his intellect.

223
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:08,917
Did you think you could just
run away without paying?

224
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,824
I'll make sure you rot in jail.

225
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:14,614
Sorry, but you will never be
able to put me behind bars.

226
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:17,517
I take it you're not
familiar with De Seiko vs.

227
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:18,960
Argento, 1982?

228
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:21,617
Based on the results of that case,

229
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:26,465
it is highly likely that the court will
determine I acted out of basic necessity.

230
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:31,817
Bucciarati, please, you have to
do something about this child!

231
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,730
Hmm.

232
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,760
How interesting.

233
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:37,977
Fugo's visit happened to
occur right as Bucciarati

234
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,648
was pondering the
formation of his own team.

235
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:42,830
There.

236
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,489
Now you basically know
everything about me.

237
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:47,780
You can stop feeling sorry for me.

238
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:50,140
I'm not unhappy if that helps.

239
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:52,997
I see. Hmm.

240
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,551
I don't think you're here today by chance.

241
00:13:57,140 --> 00:14:00,237
Would you join my team, Panakata Fugo?

242
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:02,280
Your intellect is one of a kind.

243
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,180
I'm sorry, but I can't.

244
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:10,560
I've got nothing against becoming a
mafioso, but I've made up my mind.

245
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:15,280
It's for the best if I go it
alone in life. Oh? Why's that?

246
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:16,870
I told you.

247
00:14:16,953 --> 00:14:20,220
When I lose my temper, my
darkest thoughts take over.

248
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:23,237
If I acquiesced and
joined up with your team,

249
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,537
I couldn't guarantee I wouldn't kill you.

250
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:28,796
Well, lucky for you, I'm
willing to bet on those odds.

251
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,177
Leave your past and come with me.

252
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:34,480
I swear you and your
talents will be respected.

253
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:37,120
